{
  "tema": 7060,
  "slug": "se-me-olvido",
  "titulo": "The accidental se with an indirect object pronoun",
  "subtitulo": "Se me rompió el vaso. Se nos acabó la leche.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "For accidents and unplanned events: se + indirect pronoun (me, te, le, nos, les) + verb agreeing with the thing: se me cayó el celular, se le cayeron las llaves. It takes the blame off the person.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "se +",
            "me / te / le / nos / les",
            "+ verb + thing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **thing** is the subject, so the verb agrees with it: **se me rompió el reloj**, **se me rompieron los lentes**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The **indirect pronoun** shows who it happened to."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The effect: it was an **accident**, not on purpose. **Perdí mi celular** puts the blame on me; **se me perdió el celular** makes it sound like the phone got lost on its own."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "caérsele",
              "texto": "_to drop_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "rompérsele",
              "texto": "_to break (by accident)_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "olvidársele",
              "texto": "_to forget_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "acabársele",
              "texto": "_to run out of_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "perdérsele",
              "texto": "_to lose_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "quemársele",
              "texto": "_to burn_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "quedársele",
              "texto": "_to leave behind_"
            },
            {
              "forma": "descomponérsele",
              "texto": "_to break down_ (machines)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: blame the object. **Se me cayó**: it fell, I just happened to be there."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Ayer ==se me rompió== el reloj.",
              "en": "My watch broke yesterday."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se le cayeron== los libros.",
              "en": "He dropped his books."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se nos olvidaron== las llaves.",
              "en": "We forgot the keys."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Se te está quemando== el pan!",
              "en": "Your toast is burning!"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se les van a caer== las cajas.",
              "en": "They're going to drop the boxes."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Se les perdió== el gato?",
              "en": "Did you guys lose your cat?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se nos acabó== la tinta de la impresora.",
              "en": "We ran out of printer ink."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se me quedó== el libro en la casa.",
              "en": "I left the book at home."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Se me descompuso== el carro en la carretera.",
              "en": "My car broke down on the highway."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
